<!--
  M0 exit criterion 2 (architecture.md Part II - M0): the validator catches
  10/10 seeded defects in a synthetic PINT AE invoice.

  Exactly ten defects are seeded, one per intended rule, and the rest of the
  document is deliberately clean so that the count is unambiguous. The
  accompanying .expected.json asserts match="exact", so an eleventh finding
  fails the corpus just as loudly as a missing one - over-firing is a defect
  too, and a pass/fail boolean would hide it entirely.

    1  BT-48 buyer TRN present but empty          -> CDL-PROV-041
    2  BT-31 seller TRN only 12 digits            -> CDL-PROV-043
    3  BT-151 line VAT category not in UNTDID5305 -> CDL-PROV-018
    4  BT-130 unit code is free text ("Nos.")     -> CDL-PROV-019
    5  BT-106 header total != sum of line BT-131  -> CDL-PROV-011
    6  BT-5  currency lower-case                  -> CDL-PROV-006
    7  BT-153 line item name missing              -> CDL-PROV-021
    8  BT-2  issue date in DD/MM/YYYY             -> CDL-PROV-003
    9  BT-110 tax amount carries three decimals   -> CDL-PROV-015
   10  BT-118 VAT breakdown category unmapped     -> CDL-PROV-024

  Synthetic. Every identifier is invented. The document otherwise carries the
  UAE skeleton confirmed from the FTA/MoF primary sources - schemeID 0235 on
  the endpoint, BTAE-15 = TL with its BTAE-12 authority name, and BTAE-02 as
  an 8-character transaction-type bitmask.
-->
